Amanda, you might as well go through them because we don't have that many additional people.

00:00:43.970 --> 00:00:45.730
Okay. Joe, would you like to go first?

00:00:46.495 --> 00:00:48.575
>> Yeah. Yeah. I'll go ahead and go first.

00:00:49.615 --> 00:00:50.655
First, I wanna

00:00:51.295 --> 00:00:54.735
thank you all for all the hard work you guys have been doing on the budget

00:00:54.735 --> 00:00:56.895
and the transparency with that.

00:00:57.295 --> 00:01:04.000
With being a new town resident, it's it's good to see that type of transparency, especially during these times.

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:07.360
But I wanted to touch on something different.

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:08.880
And

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:16.375
I'm not the pitchfork and torch kind of guy, so I kind of gathered my thoughts down, wrote them down, so I'm just gonna read them out.

00:01:16.855 --> 00:01:17.415
But

00:01:17.895 --> 00:01:19.815
so my name is Joseph Goblin.

00:01:19.815 --> 00:01:22.055
I'm a resident here in Andover.

00:01:22.455 --> 00:01:24.775
Me and my family moved to Andover because,

00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:28.330
well, while home shopping, we fell in love with the area.

00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:31.770
But we liked that we saw Lake Road neighbors out walking,

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:40.250
jogging, bike riding, taking their dogs on walks. Just about everyone waves to each other. It's a pretty friendly area. So

00:01:40.805 --> 00:01:47.125
we liked it. We fell in love with it. We did our research. School ratings were great. Reasonable tax rate,

00:01:47.445 --> 00:01:48.485
low crime,

00:01:48.725 --> 00:01:51.445
and the lake amenities nearby. We love that.

00:01:52.485 --> 00:01:57.070
Alright. This meant a lot to us, and we decided to to move in. We moved in last November,

00:01:57.390 --> 00:01:59.230
and we we plan on staying.

00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:03.310
Fast forward now. We're on Lake Road. We love our neighborhood.

00:02:03.870 --> 00:02:06.110
But recently, we've made some concerning

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:10.590
or some concerning observations of some of the current traffic habits, which

00:02:11.335 --> 00:02:15.655
I'll get into. I figured that's a sensitive topic with some folks.

00:02:16.615 --> 00:02:19.495
But we've made some concerning observations,

00:02:20.135 --> 00:02:20.615
and

00:02:20.935 --> 00:02:21.575
some

00:02:21.815 --> 00:02:22.855
of the observations

00:02:23.095 --> 00:02:24.215
have to do with speed.

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:28.660
And I'm not talking about the occasional speeder. I know that happens.

00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:31.300
It's the constant flow

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:31.860
of

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:32.980
speeders

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:34.660
on Lake Road specifically.

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:39.140
So this consists of residents, non residents,

00:02:39.635 --> 00:02:40.835
contractors,

00:02:41.795 --> 00:02:46.355
triaxials, trucks, cars, motorcycles, the postal service, UPS, FedEx.

00:02:47.075 --> 00:02:50.755
It seems like everybody has a little bit of skin in the game.

00:02:51.715 --> 00:02:52.675
And because of that,

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:55.960
I can't let my kids play in the front yard.

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:58.280
My property is a little bit sloped,

00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:05.160
and the scenario of the ball rolling into the road is all too real. And I know if that were to happen,

00:03:06.215 --> 00:03:10.375
there'd be a likelihood that one of my kids would most likely be struck.

00:03:11.335 --> 00:03:15.735
So just crossing the street to get to the mail turns into a game of fraud, unfortunately,

00:03:15.735 --> 00:03:16.295
sometimes.

00:03:16.855 --> 00:03:20.615
I've almost been taken out by side mirrors with cars going 30 plus miles an hour.

00:03:21.890 --> 00:03:28.370
I've taken kids on walks, which turns into a nightmare when two cars pass by the opposite directions

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:31.970
and usually well above the posted speed limit.

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:37.245
And lastly, for the same reasons as noted previously, taking my child out on her bike

00:03:37.485 --> 00:03:39.325
becomes a dangerous task.

00:03:39.485 --> 00:03:43.405
She's still on her training wheels, and her margin for error is

00:03:43.725 --> 00:03:46.445
very low if she were to tip over

00:03:46.765 --> 00:03:48.365
while we're riding her bikes.

00:03:49.245 --> 00:03:53.510
No activity feel safe in the late mode, unfortunately.

00:03:54.710 --> 00:04:00.150
And I've seen people yelling at cars. I'm not the one to yell at somebody or wave my hands,

00:04:00.390 --> 00:04:03.510
but I've seen other people become pretty upset.

00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:05.030
So

00:04:06.105 --> 00:04:07.465
with that being said,

00:04:08.665 --> 00:04:09.465
you know,

00:04:09.785 --> 00:04:13.145
there are those that argue that the road's not the place for people,

00:04:13.305 --> 00:04:14.665
and I would disagree.

00:04:14.985 --> 00:04:17.625
Neighborhood roads have historically and culturally

00:04:17.705 --> 00:04:21.305
been a place where children play, bike, skateboard, rollerblade, etcetera.

00:04:22.180 --> 00:04:25.060
That's how I grew up. I grew up in Groton

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:30.100
when I was younger, and we were kind of out and about. We'd ride our scooters, ride our bikes,

00:04:31.060 --> 00:04:33.300
and we'd clear out when the car came.

00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:34.820
Unfortunately,

00:04:34.820 --> 00:04:38.045
here, I think it's a little bit more difficult because

00:04:38.445 --> 00:04:39.245
there's

00:04:39.245 --> 00:04:42.845
a lot more speeding going on than what I remember as a kid.

00:04:43.725 --> 00:04:47.005
And with the lake so close by, this can't be our attitude.

00:04:47.645 --> 00:04:50.445
I think we all benefit from safe neighborhood roads.

00:04:51.110 --> 00:04:51.830
And

00:04:52.710 --> 00:04:54.070
I'm sure that others

00:04:55.110 --> 00:04:57.510
feel the same way in other parts of the town.

00:04:58.230 --> 00:04:59.750
In light of these observations,

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:05.110
I decided to reach out to a very small portion of the community representing about 20% of Andover's population

00:05:05.745 --> 00:05:08.305
on Facebook, social media platform.

00:05:09.025 --> 00:05:09.585
And

00:05:10.225 --> 00:05:18.865
I asked them if they noticed this traffic trend. And I know a couple of select men that are on tonight have been there and read some of the comments that have been made.

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:23.230
Some people, you know, they they get angry. They don't have a solution,

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:26.190
and, you know, they just kinda spill it out there.

00:05:27.310 --> 00:05:30.510
But I wanted to come to you guys officially and,

00:05:30.910 --> 00:05:32.510
you know, address those concerns.

00:05:33.635 --> 00:05:37.475
People gave out dozens of examples of how people blow through stop signs.

00:05:37.955 --> 00:05:43.875
They speed, obviously, pass pedestrians dangerously close, and not just on Lake Road, but other parts of Andover.

00:05:44.995 --> 00:05:51.040
There were some, which this is hearsay, unless it's already on the record. I I don't know. I am new to town.

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:59.440
That they say they've approached the trooper and the selectmen in the past looking for solutions. And from their perceptions, the status quo has continued. Nothing's been done.

00:06:00.235 --> 00:06:02.875
Others mentioned how this board of selectmen

00:06:03.515 --> 00:06:04.475
is new

00:06:04.875 --> 00:06:07.435
and with the interest of in hearing about the problem.

00:06:07.915 --> 00:06:15.950
We, as a community, have identified it. It's a public safety problem in its simplest form and an opportunity to make Andover neighborhoods a little more safe for everyone,

00:06:16.590 --> 00:06:19.470
especially as we approach summer and more people are out

00:06:20.030 --> 00:06:21.630
enjoying the weather.

00:06:22.270 --> 00:06:27.470
And while it might be easy to say the trooper will take care of the brush off the issue because there is not a clear solution,

00:06:27.790 --> 00:06:32.635
I'm contending that there might be a solution in developing a public safety committee

00:06:32.955 --> 00:06:33.595
with

00:06:34.155 --> 00:06:37.595
some of the board of selectmen to address the issue.

00:06:38.475 --> 00:06:43.675
Stop sign speed bumps, radar speed limit signs, more trooper presence ticketing are all components of the solution,

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:45.720
but organized,

00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:47.560
collaborative approach is necessary.

00:06:48.200 --> 00:06:54.360
The trooper can't single handedly provide a solution. In fact, once you pass the trooper on six or three sixteen,

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:59.160
it's the safe bet you can speed without consequence for the remainder of your travel within town.

00:06:59.960 --> 00:07:11.665
So this isn't something that I think is gonna be solved instantly. I don't think there's any magic formula to control individual behavior. I think there will always be those who think about themselves and and continue to go about their ways.

00:07:12.730 --> 00:07:17.130
But I know that there's mitigation and engineering controls that can be implemented over time

00:07:17.450 --> 00:07:24.730
and in course to encourage drivers to obey the posted speed limit and create a safer neighborhood frequented by pedestrians.

00:07:25.210 --> 00:07:30.945
So this is my official plea for the record to form a public safety committee with a minimum of two selectmen

00:07:30.945 --> 00:07:37.265
to address the speeding problem or any subsequent action deemed more appropriate to address the problem.

00:07:37.505 --> 00:07:39.905
And I understand that these things cost money,

00:07:40.545 --> 00:07:42.785
and I know that it's not gonna be done immediately.

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:46.440
And I think that is good to be expected.

00:07:46.760 --> 00:07:49.800
But I think that would be money well spent in the future,

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:52.760
whether that's next year or the year after.

00:07:53.480 --> 00:07:55.240
So thank you for your time and consideration,

00:07:55.485 --> 00:07:59.485
and I'll forward my thoughts to you guys to have on record.

00:08:00.125 --> 00:08:01.085
All right. Thank you.

